---
import CaseLayout from '../../layouts/CaseLayout.astro';
import SectionTitle from '../../components/SectionTitle.astro';
import CaseFeature from '../../components/CaseFeature.astro';
import GridLines from '../../components/GridLines.astro';
import Pic from '../../components/Pic.astro';

const img = '/images/case-cognitive';
---

<CaseLayout
  title="Cognitive Structuring — Alex Abrosov"
  description="A planning tool for merger and acquisition processes, with taxonomy integration and automated reporting."
  accent="var(--color-accent-green)"
>
  <!-- Start screen -->
  <div class="case-opening">
    <section class="case-hero container case-grid">
      <div class="case-hero-left">
        <div class="case-hero-text">
          <p class="t-subtitle" data-reveal>2024</p>
          <h1 class="case-hero-title t-h1" data-reveal>Cognitive <br /><em>Structuring</em></h1>
          <p class="case-hero-intro t-body-2" data-reveal>
            This tool facilitates planning merger and acquisition (M&amp;A) processes and enables
            comparison of different merger scenarios. It is part of the client&rsquo;s global M&amp;A
            platform and emphasizes taxonomy integration. The service automatically generates reports
            used to create client proposals and develop departmental integration strategies.
          </p>
        </div>

        <dl class="case-meta" data-reveal>
          <div>
            <div class="case-meta-group">
              <dt class="t-subtitle">Client</dt>
              <dd class="t-body">A Big Four accounting firm</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="case-meta-group">
              <dt class="t-subtitle">Industry</dt>
              <dd class="t-body">FinTech</dd>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt class="t-subtitle">Services</dt>
            <dd class="t-body">
              Discovery &amp; Research<br />UX/UI Design<br />Vibe Coding<br />Design System<br />User Testing
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt class="t-subtitle">Responsibilities</dt>
            <dd class="t-body">Product Design<br />Management</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </div>

      <div class="case-tile case-hero-tile" data-reveal>
        <Pic eager src={`${img}/hero-screen.png`} alt="Cognitive Structuring process map builder" />
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="case-screen">
      <Pic src={`${img}/screen.png`} alt="Cognitive Structuring running on a laptop" />
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Challenge -->
  <section class="case-section container case-grid challenge">
    <SectionTitle title="Challenge" />
    <p class="col-wide case-intro t-body-2" data-reveal>
      The client&rsquo;s merger and acquisition planning tools were outdated, significantly lowering
      employee productivity. The main challenge was to create a new product that streamlined workflows
      while preserving key functions of the existing product. It also needed to integrate with the
      client&rsquo;s platform, making it essential to maintain a familiar user experience.
    </p>
    <ol class="col-wide case-goals" data-reveal>
      <li>
        <p class="t-h3">1.</p>
        <p class="t-body">Boost user effectiveness with an intuitive, scalable tool.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p class="t-h3">2.</p>
        <p class="t-body">Ensure integration compatibility with the company&rsquo;s other M&amp;A products.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p class="t-h3">3.</p>
        <p class="t-body">Develop customizable summary reports with filtering and export functionality.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
    <div class="case-tile case-challenge-tile" data-reveal>
      <Pic class="badge-img" src={`${img}/badge.png`} alt="Client mark" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Solution -->
  <section class="case-section container case-grid solution">
    <SectionTitle title="Solution" />
    <div class="col-wide case-solution-intro" data-reveal>
      <p class="t-body-2">
        After discussions with stakeholders and users, we streamlined the homepage to focus on core
        tasks&mdash;creating and managing company structures and generating reports. To meet users&rsquo;
        need to view all taxonomies at once, we combined them into a single, customizable, and
        filterable view. For statistics, three concepts were developed, with one approved after testing.
      </p>
      <p class="case-tags t-button">
        <span>Structure, Table, Heatmap Views</span><i></i><span>Comparison</span><i></i>
        <span>Statistics</span><i></i><span>Reports Builder</span><i></i>
        <span>AI Data Generation</span><i></i><span>Admin Modules</span>
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="col-text solution-feature" data-reveal>
      <div class="case-block">
        <h3 class="t-subtitle">/ Builder Features</h3>
        <p class="t-body">
          Data can be presented in three formats, enabling filtering, visualization, and evaluation of
          potential mergers or department maturity levels within companies.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="case-tile case-solution-tile" data-reveal>
      <Pic src={`${img}/solution.jpg`} alt="Process map builder interface" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Solution details -->
  <div class="feature-stack">
    <CaseFeature
      index={1}
      title="Metadata"
      body="Each taxonomy element includes relevant data based on its level, such as process objectives, number of involved employees, technologies, leadership, and other key information."
      image={`${img}/feature-1.jpg`}
      alt="Taxonomy element metadata"
      frame={{ left: '11.6%', top: '7%', width: '76.8%' }}
    />
    <CaseFeature
      index={2}
      title="Taxonomy Creation"
      body="The product enables creating company structures in four ways: from scratch, using existing companies, following industry standards, or leveraging AI based on key required characteristics."
      image={`${img}/feature-2.jpg`}
      alt="Taxonomy creation options"
      frame={{ left: '11.6%', top: '7%', width: '76.8%' }}
    />
    <CaseFeature
      index={3}
      title="Reports"
      body="Visualizes key performance indicators and relationships between departments. Data can be displayed for both the current state and projected future state after changes are made. The product automatically generates a detailed PDF presentation that consultants use as pitch materials for their clients."
      image={`${img}/feature-3.jpg`}
      alt="Reports and performance indicators"
      frame={{ left: '11.3%', top: '7%', width: '77.3%' }}
    />
  </div>

  <!-- Results -->
  <section class="case-section container case-grid case-results results">
    <GridLines local />
    <SectionTitle title="Results" />
    <p class="col-wide case-intro t-body-2" data-reveal>
      The product received positive user feedback and has become the standard tool for consultants
      working on M&amp;A projects. After several releases, users praised the convenience of the new tool
      and the streamlined workflow enabled by the library of pre-built taxonomies and AI-generated
      metadata.
    </p>
    <ol class="col-wide case-outcomes outcomes-3" data-reveal>
      <li>
        <p class="t-h3">1.</p>
        <h3 class="t-subtitle">Proposal preparation process has accelerated by 34%</h3>
        <p class="t-body">
          The tool significantly boosted consultant productivity, reducing the time from project start
          to delivering the final client deck by an average of 34% compared to the previous product.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p class="t-h3">2.</p>
        <h3 class="t-subtitle">Increased client conversion rate by ~6%</h3>
        <p class="t-body">
          The percentage of successful client deals increased by 6%, with users highlighting the
          automatic generation of ready-to-use client presentation decks as the key contributing feature.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p class="t-h3">3.</p>
        <h3 class="t-subtitle">Successfully integrated artificial intelligence</h3>
        <p class="t-body">
          Statistics show that the auto-fill and auto-generation of taxonomies features have become
          constant assistants for users, significantly speeding up their workflow.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>
</CaseLayout>

<style>
  .challenge {
    min-height: 1083px;
  }

  .case-challenge-tile {
    margin-top: 126px;
  }

  .case-challenge-tile :global(.badge-img) {
    position: static;
    width: 130px;
    height: 130px;
    border-radius: 50%;
  }

  .solution {
    min-height: 1565px;
  }

  .solution-feature {
    margin-top: 140px;
  }

  .solution-feature .case-block > * + * {
    margin-top: 16px;
  }

  .case-solution-tile {
    margin-top: 90px;
  }

  .case-solution-tile img {
    width: 71.5%;
    border-radius: 18px;
  }

  .results {
    min-height: 835px;
  }

  /* This case reports three outcomes rather than four */
  .outcomes-3 {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    margin-top: 48px;
  }

  /* ---- Tablet and mobile ---- */
  @media (max-width: 1180px) {
    .challenge,
    .solution,
    .results {
      min-height: 0;
    }

    .solution-feature {
      grid-column: 1 / -1;
      margin-top: 64px;
    }

    .case-solution-tile {
      margin-top: 64px;
    }

    .case-solution-tile img {
      width: 88%;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 767px) {
    /* This tile uses a 126px lead on desktop, off the mobile scale. */
    .case-challenge-tile {
      margin-top: 100px;
    }
    .solution-feature {
      margin-top: 48px;
    }

    .case-solution-tile {
      margin-top: 48px;
    }
  }
</style>